WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:02.868
-Today is Friday, and that's
usually when I catch up

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:03.868
on some personal stuff.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:04.934
I check my inbox.

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:06.400
I return some emails,
and of course,

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.567
I send out thank you notes,
and I was running a bit behind.

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:09.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.400
So I thought
you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.767
I'd like to write out my weekly
thank you notes right now.

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:14.234
Is that okay with you?

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:16.067
James, can I get some thank you
note writing music, please?

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:18.968
[ Gentle music playing ]

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:20.534
-Oh, he's giggly.

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:21.901
He's giggly tonight.

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:23.400
-It's a bobblehead James.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.167
-Giggly James.
-They call him Mr. Laugh-tastic.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:29.200
-You know how James laughs?
-How?

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.133
Let me cut to James.
He goes like --

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:33.801
hoo-hoo-hoo-ha-ha-hey!

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.133
Hoo-hoo-hoo-ha-ha-hey!

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.734
[ Continues goofy laughter ]

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:38.534
"I play the piano, hey."

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:41.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.767
-Hoo-hoo-hoo-ha-ha!

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:45.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:47.267
[ Gentle piano music ]

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:50.467
-Thank you, Mother's Day,
for giving people the chance

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:51.834
to send their mom an e-card

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:54.033
that will take her 5 hours
to figure out how to open.

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:55.033
[ Applause ]

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:58.567
Why would you?

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:01.133
-Oh, you got me an e-card?

00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:03.934
-[ Chuckles ] I like this one.

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:05.100
♪♪

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.534
-Thank you, Doctor Strange.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:08.901
With the ring and the hair,

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:11.701
you're basically
the Paulie Walnuts of the MCU.

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:13.033
[ Applause ]

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:18.601
"Hey, this guy's breaking
my Infinity Stones over here."

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:22.834
-"Oh, I open the portal, hey."

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:26.033
-Ohh.
-"Hey, MCU. Heyy."

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:29.434
-"Hey, MC-you!"

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:32.334
-CBD!

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:35.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:38.200
-Thank you, Kentucky Derby hats
for making it look

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.000
like you wandered
into the back of a pizzeria

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.400
at the exact wrong moment.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.701
It's like, ba-ba-dee -- oh!

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:46.267
[ Applause ]

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.300
-Thank you,

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.267
Thomas' new line of
muffin tops, for being honest

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:58.534
about what's going to happen
to my stomach after I eat you.

00:01:58.534 --> 00:02:00.534
[ Applause ]

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:10.601
Thank you, Star Wars puns that
make me remember the date,

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:13.400
like May the Fourth
and Revenge of the Sixth.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.734
You're fun, but now I got
nothing between now and --

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:19.634
[ Laughing ]

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.834
Between now
and Octobi-wan Kenober.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:27.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.000
-Come on, dude.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.934
Come on, man.
It's Octobi-wan. Woo!

00:02:33.934 --> 00:02:35.567
-Octobi-wan Kenober.

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.767
-Yeah, like Roctober. Yeah.

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:42.734
-Thank you, wedding gift
registries for showing me

00:02:42.734 --> 00:02:44.901
that our friendship is
definitely not worth a Vitamix,

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:47.868
but is maybe worth
some bedsheets and a spatula.

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:50.033
Maybe?

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:51.868
[ Applause ]

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:58.067
Thank you, mint juleps,
for sounding cute, but really

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:00.534
meaning Grandma has been
pounding bourbon since noon.

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:02.467
There you have it, everybody.
Those are our thank you notes.

